  "body": "Closes #922\nClaim: mac/M1\nAuthor model: Claude Opus 5.5 (mac/M1-c922-opus); docs fix commit by Claude Opus 5.5 (mac/M1)\nReviewer model: Fable 5.1 (mac/M1-c922-fable)\n\n### What\nThe `img3.super-h.fr` medium rendition, captured for real (operator's go, 2026-11-18): **one** upload of a generated neutral test pattern (2400×1600, no EXIF/APP13), then cookie-less GETs of its `.md.`, full-size and `.th.` URLs, each with and without `Referer: https://forum.hardware.fr/`.\n\n- `U03`: the upload answer, redacted exactly as `U01` (`delete_hash`, delete token → `REDACTED`; image id → `AbCdE`; file number → `1234567890`). The API key was read from the git-ignored `Secrets.xcconfig` into an environment variable and never written anywhere.\n- `U03a`-`U03f`: meta only (status, type, size, dimensions).\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §LOT-056 « Medium rendition » moves from **code** to **verified**: `<name>.md.<ext>` minus `.md.` is the full image; img3's `.th.` thumbnails verified too; img3 has **no Referer gate** (bytes identical with and without). Observed: the host stored the image at 1200×800 (medium 400×267, thumb 120×120); when the host makes a medium is not established.\n- LOT-056 spec: the medium paragraph marked verified; its Fixtures section names U01–U03.\n- Test `RehostClientCaptureTests.theCapturedLargeUploadGivesAMediumThatLeadsBackToTheFullImage` decodes `U03` and checks `ImageHostTable.standard.fullSizeURL` takes the medium and the thumbnail back to the full URL; red with `.md.` removed from `ImageHostTable.swift:20`.\n\nThe test image stays on img3 as a reference (operator, 2026-11-18).\n\n### Checks\n`swift test` (HFRKit) green; `anonymize.py check --corpus` 767/767 clean; fixture tests 403 OK; pre-commit. Leak checks by the author and, independently, by Fable (key in raw/%/base64/hex, delete hash/token/url, real ids, IP, e-mail): none in the committed files or messages.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n",
